          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em differential function complex
            (
            %a{:href => "#HopkinsSinger"}> HopkinsSinger
            ) is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            s for
            %em generalized
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology
            theories:
          %p
            roughly, given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability"} representing
            a given
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology theory
            %em differential function complex
            over any given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            whose
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplices"} simplices
            are triples consisting of
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo :
                        %mi U
                        %mo ×
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi k
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : U \times \Delta^k \to E_{n}
            %li
              %p
                a smooth
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ×
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \times \Delta^k
                whose corresponding real cohomology class (under the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+theorem"} de Rham theorem
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                along
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %li
              %p
                an explicit
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coboundary"} coboundary
                in real cohomology exhibiting this fact.
          %p
            (More precisely, in order for this construction to yield not just a single
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            (which will be a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            object, there are conditons on the dependency of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            on the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+vector"} tangent vector
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
          %p
            When applied to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+spectrum"} Eilenberg-MacLane spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K\mathbb{Z}
            this construction reproduces, on cohomology classes,
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BU"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B U
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            it gives
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+K-theory"} differential K-theory
          %p
            See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "differential+cohomology+diagram#HopkinsSingerCoefficients"} differential cohomology diagram –Hopkins-Singer coefficients
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %h3#cocycles_with_values_in_graded_vector_spaces Cocycles with values in graded vector spaces
          %p
            For the present purposes it will be convenient to collect
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V = V^\bullet
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
              over the
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                  a
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo ,
                        %mi V
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi n
                        %mo :
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊕
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo +
                            %mi j
                            %mo =
                            %mi n
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo ,
                        %msup
                          %mi V
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        C^\bullet(E, V)^n := \oplus_{i + j = n} C^i(E, V^j)
              %li
                %p and so on
          %p (…)
          %h3#differential_functions Differential functions
          #DifferentialFunctions.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p For
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                  a
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ι
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi Z
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota \in Z^n(E,\mathbb{R})
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                  for real-valued
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+cohomology"} singular cohomology
                  on
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi E
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %p
              a
              %strong differential function
              on a smooth
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              with values in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ι
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (E,\iota)
              is a triple
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi h
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (c,h,\omega)
              with
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo :
                        %mi U
                        %mo →
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c : U \to E
                  a continuous map;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ω
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \in \Omega^n(S)
                  a smooth
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
                  on
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi h
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h \in C^{n-1}(U,\mathbb{R})
                  a cochain in real cohomology on (the topological space underlying)
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %p
              such that in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Z
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z^n(S,\mathbb{R})
              of singular cochains the equation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi c
                      %mo *
                    %mi ι
                    %mo +
                    %mi δ
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\omega = c^*\iota + \delta h
            %p holds, where
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ω
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                  is here regarded as a singular cochain (that sends a chain to the integral of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ω
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                  over it, as discussed at
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+theorem"} de Rham theorem
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi δ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
                  denotes the coboundary operator,(the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+complex"} Moore complex
                  differential of the
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+simplicial+complex"} singular simplicial complex
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#HopkinsSinger"}> HopkinsSinger, def.4.1
            ).
          %p
            In words this is: a continuous map to the topological space together with a
            %em smooth
            refinement of the pullback of the chosen singular cochain.
          %h3#differential_function_complexes Differential function complexes
          #DifferentialFunctionComplex.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p For
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                  be a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                  and
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ι
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi Z
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota \in Z^n(E,\mathbb{R})
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                  for real-valued
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+cohomology"} singular cohomology
                  on
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                  a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %p
              the
              %strong differential function complex
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ι
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (E,\iota)^U
            %p
              of all differential functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ι
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \to (X,\iota)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              whose
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
